1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,220
LINDA: Hello, Linda speaking.

2
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:07,269
MATT: Oh hi, Linda. This is Matt Brooks.

3
00:00:07,269 --> 00:00:10,280
Alex White gave me your number

4
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:14,890
He said you'd be able to give me some advice about moving to Banford.

5
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:20,660
LINDA: Yes, Alex did mention you. How can I help?

6
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:25,520
MATT: Well, first of all - which area to live in?

7
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:28,740
LINDA: Well, I live in Dalton

8
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:37,030
which is a really nice suburb. Not too expensive, and there's a nice park.

9
00:00:37,030 --> 00:00:43,210
MATT: Sounds good. Do you know how much it would be to rent a two bedroom flat there?

10
00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:51,789
LINDA: Yeah, you should be able to get something reasonable for 850 pounds per month.

11
00:00:51,789 --> 00:00:54,649
That's what people typically pay.

12
00:00:54,649 --> 00:01:03,800
You certainly wouldn't want to pay more than 900 pounds. That doesn't include bills or anything.

13
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:06,060
MATT: No. That sounds alright.

14
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:12,840
I'll definitely have a look there. Are the transport links easy from where you live?

15
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:18,515
LINDA: Well, I'm very lucky. I work in the city centre

16
00:01:18,555 --> 00:01:24,470
so I don't have to use public transport. I go by bike

17
00:01:24,470 --> 00:01:30,130
MATT: Oh, I wish I could do that. Is it safe to cycle around the city?

18
00:01:30,130 --> 00:01:36,971
LINDA: Yes, it's fine. And it keeps me fit. Anyway,

19
00:01:37,031 --> 00:01:42,147
driving to work in the city centre would be a nightmare

20
00:01:42,147 --> 00:01:50,730
because there's hardly any parking. And the traffic during the rush hour can be bad.

21
00:01:50,730 --> 00:01:57,100
MATT: I'd be working from home but I'd have to go to London one or two days a week.

22
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:03,555
LINDA: Oh, that's perfect. Getting to London is no problem.

23
00:02:03,555 --> 00:02:11,300
There's a fast train every 30 minutes which only takes 45 minutes.

24
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:13,020
MATT: That's good.

25
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:18,404
LINDA: Yeah, the train service isn't bad during the week.

26
00:02:18,404 --> 00:02:25,402
And they run quite late at night. It's weekends that are a problem.

27
00:02:25,402 --> 00:02:29,660
They're always doing engineering work

28
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:36,170
and you have to take a bus to Hadham and pick up the train there,

29
00:02:36,170 --> 00:02:40,740
which is really slow. But other than that

30
00:02:41,260 --> 00:02:45,860
Banford's a great place to live. I've never been happier.

31
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:50,440
LINDA: There are some nice restaurants in the city centre

32
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:56,120
and a brand new cinema which has only been open a couple of months

33
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:59,600
There's a good arts centre too.

34
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:02,760
MATT: Sounds like Banford's got it all.

35
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:10,433
LINDA: Yes! We're really lucky. There are lots of really good aspects to living here.

36
00:03:10,433 --> 00:03:18,618
The schools are good and the hospital here is one of the best in the country.

37
00:03:18,618 --> 00:03:23,734
Everyone I know who's been there's had a positive experience.

38
00:03:23,734 --> 00:03:32,430
Oh, I can give you the name of my dentist too in Bridge Street, if you're interested.

39
00:03:32,430 --> 00:03:39,080
I've been going to him for years and I've never had any problems.

40
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:42,200
MATT: Oh, OK. Thanks!

41
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:46,550
LINDA: I'll find his number and send it to you.

42
00:03:46,550 --> 00:03:50,100
MATT: Thanks, that would be really helpful.

43
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:54,040
LINDA: Are you planning to visit Banford soon?

44
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:57,980
MATT: Yes. My wife and I are both coming next week

45
00:03:58,820 --> 00:04:02,040
We want to make some appointments with estate agents.

46
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:06,570
LINDA: I could meet you if you like and show you around.

47
00:04:06,570 --> 00:04:10,630
MATT: Are you sure? We'd really appreciate that.

48
00:04:10,630 --> 00:04:18,050
LINDA: Either a Tuesday or Thursday is good for me, after 5.30.

49
00:04:18,050 --> 00:04:24,680
MATT: Thursday's preferable - Tuesday I need to get home before 6 pm.

50
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:31,460
LINDA: OK. Great. Let me know which train you're catching

51
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:35,178
and I'll meet you in the cafe outside.

52
00:04:35,178 --> 00:04:42,760
You can't miss it. It's opposite the station and next to the museum.

53
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:50,700
MATT: Brilliant. I'll text you next week then. Thanks so much for all the advice.

54
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:54,790
LINDA: No problem. I'll see you next week.
